================================================================================
FFmpeg (bundled program: resources/engine/bin/ffmpeg, ffprobe)
================================================================================
The desktop app (Linux AppImage, Windows installer) ships FFmpeg's `ffmpeg` and
`ffprobe` executables. They run as separate programs: Hermes Studio starts them
as subprocesses and never links to them. The Hermes Studio code stays MIT.

Build: BtbN FFmpeg-Builds, static "gpl" variant, FFmpeg 9.0 branch
  Version string:  n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068  (`ffmpeg -version` prints
                   "n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068-20260930")
  Release:         autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08
                   https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/tag/autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08
  Linux asset:     https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/download/autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08/ffmpeg-n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068-linux64-gpl-9.0.tar.xz
                   sha256 68ee646831adaae2495618346f3bba94ff207ff83bbd34d643e7004730d66269
  Windows asset:   https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/download/autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08/ffmpeg-n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068-win64-gpl-9.0.zip
                   sha256 a0e45723c72141975f51d8666302e614711745f3102b704ca3f82c897a58d278

License: GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later).
  The build is configured with --enable-gpl --enable-version3. Full text:
  licenses/FFmpeg-GPL.txt (shipped in the app next to this file).
  The build includes GPL-only libraries, among them x264, x265, xavs2, davs2,
  Xvid, vid.stab, Rubber Band, libdvdread/libdvdnav, frei0r and AviSynth, plus
  libass and other LGPL/BSD/MIT libraries. `ffmpeg -version` prints the full
  configure line.

Corresponding source:
  FFmpeg source at the exact commit of this build (17 commits after the
  n9.0.2 tag, so the tag alone is not the matching source):
    https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/2a571b606854520cf89804d8030c8b328e621689
    https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/archive/2a571b606854520cf89804d8030c8b328e621689.tar.gz
  Build scripts (pin every library's source and its configure flags):
    https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/tree/autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08
  Starting with v0.5.3, each Hermes Studio release also attaches copies of the
  FFmpeg source and the build scripts above. FFmpeg legal notes:
  https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

================================================================================
PyAV and the FFmpeg libraries it bundles (used by faster-whisper)
================================================================================
The app's Python engine includes PyAV, which faster-whisper uses to decode
audio. PyAV runs inside the engine's Python process.

  PyAV 18.1.0 (BSD-3-Clause)  https://github.com/PyAV-Org/PyAV/tree/v18.1.0
                              https://pypi.org/project/av/18.1.0/
  faster-whisper (MIT)        https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper

The PyAV 18.1.0 wheels bundle shared FFmpeg libraries, built by pyav-ffmpeg:
  FFmpeg 8.1.2 (libavutil 60.26.102, libavcodec 62.28.102, libavformat 62.12.102,
  libavdevice 62.3.102, libavfilter 11.14.102, libswscale 9.5.102,
  libswresample 6.3.102); these are the values `av.library_versions` reports.
  The libraries report "LGPL version 3 or later" (LGPL-3.0-or-later; full text
  in licenses/LGPL-3.0.txt, which builds on licenses/FFmpeg-GPL.txt).
  The same wheels also bundle libx264 and libx265, which are licensed
  GPL-2.0-or-later. Treat that bundle as GPL-covered: the GPL text is in
  licenses/FFmpeg-GPL.txt.

Corresponding source:
  FFmpeg 8.1.2:      https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.1.2.tar.xz
  pyav-ffmpeg build: https://github.com/PyAV-Org/pyav-ffmpeg/tree/8.1.2-1
                     (build scripts, patches and the pinned source of every
                     bundled library; binaries at
                     https://github.com/PyAV-Org/pyav-ffmpeg/releases/tag/8.1.2-1)

================================================================================
OpenCV (opencv-python-headless 5.0.0.93, Apache-2.0) and its FFmpeg libraries
================================================================================
The app's engine installs the [reframe] extra. That wheel bundles OpenCV
(Apache-2.0) and shared FFmpeg libraries (libavcodec 62.28.101, libavformat
62.12.101, libavutil 60.26.101, libswscale 9.5.101) that report "LGPL version 2.1
or later" (full text in licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt). Third-party notices ship inside
the wheel (cv2/LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.txt).
  Source: https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python/tree/93
          https://pypi.org/project/opencv-python-headless/5.0.0.93/

The versions of PyAV and opencv-python-headless above are pinned for the app
build in packaging/engine-constraints.txt. Change this NOTICE whenever that file or the
FFMPEG_* pins in .github/workflows/desktop.yml change; tests/test_notices.py
fails otherwise.
